;;; Describe's minimal-line row on a program that states an obligation its root discharges,
;;; beside its control, `minimal-line-stated-obligation-control.ein`, the same program with
;;; the obligation and its import deleted.
;;;
;;; The program states `(total-owed likes is-a)`: every Person likes some Food. Root holds
;;; `(likes Ann Soup)`, so it discharges the one instance, Ann's, and owes nothing; with
;;; `:no-search` H is empty, so R is {∅}, root itself, and the minimal line is {∅}.
;;;
;;; On both files the row reads `1 state — ∅`, the `∅` row above it saying why (root is
;;; alive and owes nothing), and `--json-summary`'s `region.minimal.trivial` reads *∅ is in
;;; R*, true on both. A clause that read whether a node the run met owes, rather than what
;;; the program states, would be true of the control and false here, so the row has none.
;;; `ein-cli/tests/region_modes.rs` holds the pair.
;;;
;;;
;;;
(import std.algebra :symbols (total-owed))
(relation is-a  T T
  :why "{?3} is a {?4}")
(relation likes Person Food
  :why "{?3} likes {?4}")
(is-a Ann Person) (is-a Soup Food)
(total-owed likes is-a)
(likes Ann Soup)
;; Root alone: this file's question is root's verdict, and root owes nothing,
;; so R is root alone, which `(solve :no-search)` states (Q-M1f.254). A
;; `:no-hypothesis` list naming `likes`, the relation the obligation owes, is
;; refused beside it (Q-M1f.244: *"filtered obligations are nonsense by
;; definition"*), and one that leaves `likes` out filters nothing here;
;; `:no-search` says what such a list would mean.
(solve :no-search)
